{{also|granulé}}
==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*ǵerh₂-}}
Borrowed from {{bor|en|LL.|granulum}}, diminutive of {{der|en|la|granum||grain}}; for more, see {{m|en|grain}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/ˈɡɹæn.juːl/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/ˈɡɹæn.jul/|/ˈɡɹæn.jəl/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A tiny [[grain]], a small [[particle]].
# {{lb|en|biology}} A small [[structure]] in a [[cell]].
# {{lb|en|geology}} A [[particle]] from 2 to 4 [[mm]] in [[diameter]], following the [[Wentworth scale]]
# {{lb|en|astronomy}} a small [[mark]] in the [[photosphere]] of the [[sun]] caused by [[convection]] [[current]]s. See also [[Wikipedia:Granule (solar physics)]].

